    "strategy": {
      "summary": "AA REIT's decarbonization strategy for 2023 centers on a science-based approach with specific, measurable targets and concrete implementation actions. The company has committed to reducing Scope 2 greenhouse gas emissions by 42% by FY2030 from a FY2020 baseline, which aligns with the Science Based Targets initiative (SBTi) and the Paris Agreement goals to limit global warming to 1.5°C. This target was determined through a carbon baselining exercise that identified specific initiatives to reduce their carbon footprint. In FY2023, they achieved significant progress with a 25.6% reduction in scope 2 emission intensity compared to the FY2020 baseline, bringing average building GHG emission intensity down from 54.3 kgCO₂e/m² to 49.0 kgCO₂e/m².\n\nThe company has implemented several specific initiatives to drive decarbonization. They partnered with SP Group to install rooftop solar photovoltaic systems across six industrial, logistics, and warehouse properties by December 2023, which is expected to produce 14,500 megawatt-hours of energy annually and avoid over 5,900 tonnes of carbon emissions. Their carbon reduction roadmap includes replacing lifts and air conditioning/mechanical ventilation systems with more energy-efficient models across select properties, as well as enhancing procurement procedures to account for ESG considerations. The company also plans to install energy-efficient fittings and equipment in two Singapore properties in FY2024, including replacing a chiller at 135 Joo Seng and upgrading to LED lighting at 20 Gul Way.\n\nTo support this strategy, AA REIT adopted TCFD recommendations for the first time in FY2023 and implemented a phased approach toward climate reporting. They conducted their inaugural qualitative environmental risk assessment and scenario analysis to identify potential climate-related risks and opportunities, assessing transition risks under the Network for Greening the Financial System (NGFS) net zero scenario and physical risks under Intergovernmental Panel on Climate Change (IPCC) scenarios. This comprehensive approach demonstrates their commitment to managing climate-related risks while actively working toward their decarbonization targets.",
      "notes": "Multi-page strategy section found across Sustainability Report pages 87, 95, 97, and 101. Strategy focuses primarily on operational emissions (Scope 2) with specific implementation details and timelines. Includes concrete initiatives with measurable outcomes, technology investments, and governance mechanisms. Strategy connects risk management with decarbonization efforts through TCFD adoption and scenario analysis.",
      "status": null
    },
