    "targets": {
      "json": "[]",
      "notes": "No specific sustainability targets with quantifiable metrics (e.g., percentage reduction, absolute reduction values) are disclosed for 2023. The company states it is in the process of formulating science-based targets (SBTi) for Scope 1, 2, and 3 emissions (as mentioned in 'Transition plans and targets' section on page 07), but these targets have not yet been finalized or quantified for 2023. The report indicates submission to SBTi is planned for FY2024. All sustainability strategy elements (e.g., 'Invest responsibly', 'Recruit and develop talent', 'Act as a good corporate citizen') are described as principles without numerical targets. Portfolio company achievements (e.g., Evernex's avoided emissions) are not 3i Group's corporate targets.",
      "status": null
    },
    "strategy": {
      "summary": "3i Group's decarbonization strategy for 2023 centers on a structured, portfolio-wide approach to reduce emissions across their investment holdings. The company has established governance structures including an ESG Committee to advise on climate-related matters and wrote to the Science Based Targets initiative (SBTi) on April 5, 2023, to set near-term science-based targets covering Scope 1, 2, and portfolio-associated Scope 3 emissions. They are conducting comprehensive climate scenario analyses to assess physical and transition risks across their portfolio, with plans to expand TCFD reporting to include portfolio emissions metrics and develop more thorough climate risk assessments. The company is also engaging specialist consultancy to support their second phase of climate scenario analysis, expected to be completed in FY2024.\n\nThe company implements a thematic investment approach specifically targeting businesses supporting the energy transition and circular economy. They have exposure to renewable energy and waste management sectors, investing in companies developing solutions for global warming and climate change. A key example is their portfolio company Evernex, which provides circular IT solutions incorporating repair, reuse, and recycling principles to extend equipment life and reduce waste. The company is actively supporting portfolio companies like Evernex in establishing climate strategies, with Evernex joining a three-year program with ADEME to develop a climate strategy and completing the first year of the 'ACT' (Assessing Low Carbon Transition) program. Evernex's efforts have demonstrated significant emissions reductions, with analysis showing 6,570 tCO₂e of avoided emissions compared to buying new equipment.\n\nTo support implementation, 3i Group has rolled out climate training sessions for their Board of Directors and all staff, led by specialist consultants, with nearly two-thirds of employees attending. They have embedded specialist sustainability resources within their Private Equity and Infrastructure investment teams to enhance engagement with portfolio companies. The company's approach emphasizes long-term stewardship and careful portfolio construction, recognizing that their permanent capital provides a medium to long-term investment horizon that enables sustainable growth. Their strategy is integrated into their responsible investment framework, with specific focus on companies that benefit from structural growth trends including energy transition and circular economy models.",
      "notes": "Multi-page strategy section found across pages 06-07, 12, 15, and 21. Strategy focuses primarily on portfolio emissions reduction through investment selection and engagement with portfolio companies. Concrete initiatives include SBTi target setting, climate scenario analysis, thematic investment in energy transition sectors, and specific support for portfolio companies like Evernex. Limited operational emissions details provided for 3i Group itself, with greater focus on portfolio approach.",
      "status": null
    },
