    "strategy": {
      "summary": "Arion's decarbonization strategy centers on a comprehensive approach to measuring and reducing emissions across their value chain while integrating sustainability into their core corporate strategy. The company is transitioning from having a 'sustainability strategy' to a 'sustainable strategy' where corporate strategy is inherently sustainable, with sustainability as one of the strategic pillars for 2023-2025. They have already measured scope 1 and scope 2 emissions and are now shifting focus to reliably measuring scope 3 emissions, which encompasses the entire value chain. Their emission reduction plan prioritizes scope 1 and 2 emissions initially while committing to expand efforts to include scope 3 emissions for a comprehensive approach.\n\nTo reduce emissions, Arion has implemented several specific initiatives. In production processes, they've adopted a cold process for lotion production that eliminates energy-intensive heating, resulting in less energy consumption and a lower carbon footprint. For Swash® gloves manufacturing, they've improved the welding of seams to utilize less nonwoven material, effectively minimizing waste and conserving resources without compromising quality. The company has also transitioned to a predominantly electronic car park to reduce reliance on fossil fuels and has planned the installation of 500 solar panels by 2025 to harness renewable energy for operations. Additionally, they're striving to keep production waste below 4% as part of their continuous improvement in operational efficiency.\n\nSupporting these initiatives, Arion maintains an ISO 14001 certified environmental management system and conducted an energy study in 2022 to explore further reduction possibilities. The company is also exploring raw material alternatives and production process optimizations to reduce the ecological impact of their products. These efforts form a multi-faceted approach to decarbonization that addresses both immediate operational improvements and longer-term strategic shifts toward sustainability.",
      "notes": "Multi-page strategy section found across multiple pages (2, 3, 10, 15, 18, 19). Strategy focuses primarily on operational emissions (scopes 1 and 2) while expanding to scope 3. Specific implementation details provided for several initiatives including production process changes, renewable energy adoption, and emission measurement approaches. Strategy includes both current actions and planned future initiatives with concrete timelines.",
      "status": null
    },
