      "summary": "The company’s decarbonization strategy centers on a structured seven-step continuous circular process and a Climate Change Transition Plan targeting a 15% reduction in absolute Scope 1 and 2 GHG emissions by FY2035 (using FY2022 as the baseline). The strategy is organized around three strategic levers—Reduce, Produce, and Neutralise—to systematically address emissions. The seven-step process ensures rigorous implementation, beginning with establishing baselines (defining boundaries and profiling GHG emissions), identifying decarbonization opportunities, developing roadmaps based on cost-benefit analysis, executing strategies, conducting assurance on reporting, and refining improvements through continuous iteration. This framework integrates short-term action with long-term resilience, emphasizing operational efficiency and stakeholder value creation.\n\nSpecific initiatives under the Reduce lever include enhancing energy efficiency for machinery and equipment, scaling clean energy adoption, transitioning to electric vehicles, and addressing supply chain emissions. For the Produce lever, the company prioritizes on-site solar energy generation to replace fossil fuel-dependent sources. Residual emissions are managed through the Neutralise lever using Renewable Energy Certificates (REC) and carbon credits. The company tracks Scope 1, 2, and select Scope 3 emissions categories while developing mechanisms for additional Scope 3 categories, ensuring comprehensive monitoring. Progress and performance are reported annually in sustainability reports, with internal reviews validating reporting integrity and enabling iterative refinements to the climate change transition plan based on evolving business operations, environmental conditions, and market trends.",
