      "summary": "COSCO SHIPPING Lines' 2023 decarbonization strategy centers on a comprehensive approach integrating climate risk management with operational transformation. The company has established a dedicated climate risk governance structure that incorporates climate change considerations into its overall risk management system, with the Board of Directors ultimately responsible for ESG strategy. CSL has set specific environmental targets including greenhouse gas emission reduction, energy upgrade, ballast water management, exhaust emission reduction, and waste reduction targets. The strategy emphasizes both mitigating climate risks and seizing opportunities presented by the transition to low-carbon shipping.\n\nThe company is implementing several concrete initiatives to achieve its decarbonization goals. These include carrying out fuel-saving initiatives for shipping operations, connecting vessels to shore power and building green low-carbon terminals, and providing customers with Hi ECO green shipping low-carbon services. CSL has developed a carbon emission calculator for customers to measure emissions throughout the shipping process, enhancing transparency. The company has also installed desulfurization devices to reduce sulfide emissions from fuel oil and is exploring renewable energy applications to further reduce carbon footprint. These operational measures are supported by the company's ISO 14001 Environmental Management System Certification.\n\nTo support its decarbonization strategy, COSCO SHIPPING Lines has established a structured climate change risk and opportunity identification process that assesses both physical and transition risks. The company actively engages stakeholders to identify material ESG issues and has incorporated relevant indicators for energy conservation and emission reduction into executive performance evaluation. Through these integrated approaches, CSL aims to transform its shipping operations toward a more sustainable, low-carbon future while maintaining business continuity and meeting evolving customer expectations.",
