    "strategy": {
      "summary": "CEREIT's decarbonization strategy for 2023 centers on a structured approach to achieve Net Zero operational carbon emissions by 2040, with immediate focus on Scope 1 and 2 emissions. The company has developed the initial steps of its comprehensive Net Zero Strategy, which encompasses operational carbon emissions intensity reduction for its core portfolio while planning to expand targets to include Scope 3 emissions from tenants and embodied carbon. The strategy is supported by a systematic framework that includes setting specific reduction targets, implementing the Carbon Management Hierarchy (avoid, reduce, substitute, sequester, and offset), and utilizing Marginal Abatement Cost Curves to prioritize emissions reduction activities based on cost and feasibility.\n\nThe company is executing several concrete initiatives to advance its decarbonization goals. In 2023, CEREIT implemented an ESG CAPEX programme with a budget of approximately €8.2 million (€6.6 million completed), focusing on energy consumption reduction through specific measures such as installing LED lighting, BMS upgrades, smart building technology, bike parks, waste sorting units, and water leak detection devices. The company has also rolled out green leases across Europe, with 30% of lease agreements incorporating environmental clauses by year-end, requiring tenants to share utility consumption data and collaborate on joint sustainability initiatives. To support these efforts, CEREIT completed energy audits for 88% of its portfolio, with results directly feeding into annual capex planning aligned with the Net Zero Strategy.\n\nCEREIT has established robust monitoring and data infrastructure to track progress. The company utilizes the Deepki platform for property-level data collection, connecting 100% of its assets to monitor utility bills, GHG emissions, energy usage, water consumption, and waste management. The ESG data management platform enables the company to define energy and carbon pathways, plot energy and carbon pathways, and understand asset risks while capturing capex and opex program impacts. Additionally, CEREIT employs the Carbon Risk Real Estate Monitor (CRREM) tool and conducts climate scenario analysis using RCP 4.5 and other scenarios to assess physical climate-related risks to its portfolio through 2050, integrating these assessments into its risk management framework and investment decision-making processes.",
      "notes": "Multi-page strategy section found across the Sustainability Report 2023. Strategy focuses primarily on operational emissions (Scope 1 and 2) with plans to expand to Scope 3. Implementation details include specific budget figures, percentage adoption rates, and technology platforms. The strategy is supported by both operational initiatives and governance frameworks with clear timelines.",
      "status": null
    },
