    "strategy": {
      "summary": "DBS Group's 2023 decarbonization strategy centers on translating climate ambition into actionable finance solutions while supporting Asia's transition to a low-carbon economy. The bank has established a comprehensive governance structure, with the Board Sustainability Committee (chaired by CEO Piyush Gupta) providing oversight on sustainability strategy and net zero commitments. As a signatory to the Net Zero Banking Alliance since October 2021, DBS has set science-informed decarbonization targets for Scope 3 financed emissions and developed a structured approach to client engagement across seven priority sectors including Oil & Gas, Power, Shipping, and Automotive. The strategy emphasizes integrating climate mitigation and adaptation considerations into sector strategies and account planning processes, with relationship managers using tools like the Climate Analytics Tool to monitor client decarbonization progress. DBS has materially expanded client engagement with large corporate customers, with almost 90% of top emitting clients engaged having net zero plans in place. The bank is actively financing climate solutions, with sustainable financing commitments (for loans and trade finance) reaching around SGD 70 billion as of December 2023, up from SGD 51 billion the previous year. Additionally, DBS has committed up to SGD 1 billion over the next decade to improve lives of the low-income and underprivileged while fostering inclusive society. To support implementation, DBS has developed digital tools and analytical capabilities, established a Head of ESG Credit Risk position, and created the DBS Financial Planning Portal to achieve holistic financial wellness. The bank has also launched several notable initiatives including the first Sustainability-Linked Loan for global semiconductor company Nexperia, supported Indonesia's Cirebon-1 coal-fired power plant retirement through the Asian Development Bank's Energy Transition Mechanism, and advised on Singapore's Green Bond framework. DBS is strategically phasing out thermal coal financing, with plans to stop financing existing customers deriving more than 50% of revenue from thermal coal by January 2026, while maintaining support for early retirement of coal-fired power plants to meet Paris Agreement goals.",
      "notes": "Multi-page strategy section found across the sustainability report. Strategy focuses on client engagement, financing solutions, and governance structure. Includes specific case studies and implementation details. Strategy is comprehensive with concrete actions and metrics.",
      "status": null
    },
