    "targets": {
      "json": "[{\"target_reduction\": \"30% reduction\", \"target_reduction_scope\": \"Scope 1 and 2 emissions per square foot\", \"classification_of_target\": \"Intensity reduction\", \"target_year\": \"2030\", \"baseline_year\": \"2018\", \"baseline_value\": null}, {\"target_reduction\": \"68% reduction\", \"target_reduction_scope\": \"Scope 1 and 2 emissions (direct and indirect company emissions) by area\", \"classification_of_target\": \"Science-Based Target (SBTi)\", \"target_year\": \"2030\", \"baseline_year\": \"2018\", \"baseline_value\": null}, {\"target_reduction\": \"24% reduction\", \"target_reduction_scope\": \"Scope 3 emissions (indirect emissions in the value chain) by area\", \"classification_of_target\": \"Science-Based Target (SBTi)\", \"target_year\": \"2030\", \"baseline_year\": \"2018\", \"baseline_value\": null}]",
      "notes": "Three quantifiable sustainability targets found: one intensity reduction target for Digital Core REIT (Scope 1+2 emissions per square foot) and two Science-Based Targets (SBTi) for the Sponsor (Scope 1+2 and Scope 3 emissions). All targets have 2018 as baseline year and 2030 as target year. Baseline values not provided as absolute metrics; only percentage reductions against 2018 baseline are stated.",
      "status": null
    },
    "strategy": {
      "summary": "Digital Core REIT’s 2023 decarbonization strategy integrates targeted emissions reduction, operational resilience, and governance frameworks to address climate risks. The company has committed to reducing Scope 1 and 2 emissions by 30% per square foot by 2030 (against the 2018 baseline), aligned with its Sponsor’s Science-Based Targets Initiative (SBTi) goals of 68% and 24% reductions in Scope 1+2 and Scope 3 emissions, respectively, by 2030. Governance is structured to ensure accountability, with the Board overseeing sustainability strategy and ESG management, while the Management team adopts a Corporate Governance framework and sets risk appetites for climate-related material risks. The company also prioritizes TCFD-aligned disclosure across governance, strategy, risk management, and metrics to embed climate considerations into decision-making.\\n\\nTo advance decarbonization, Digital Core REIT is optimizing energy use in data centers through collaboration with its Sponsor, exploring energy-efficient solutions such as purchasing renewable energy certificates and commodity renewable energy certificates on behalf of customers. Property managers actively monitor and recalibrate temperature setpoints, prevent energy leakage, and optimize cooling systems to reduce energy consumption. Additionally, the company is studying infrastructure for resiliency and reducing reliance on diesel, while leveraging climate scenario analysis using the Intergovernmental Panel on Climate Change’s Representative Concentration Pathway to evaluate portfolio resilience against physical and transition risks.\\n\\nSupporting these efforts, Digital Core REIT aims to achieve ISO management certification for all assets under its reporting scope by 2030, further institutionalizing climate risk management. By combining targeted emissions reduction, infrastructure optimization, and robust governance, the company is advancing its decarbonization journey while addressing both operational and systemic climate challenges.",
      "notes": "Multi-page strategy section found across pages 93, 105, and 107; strategy focuses on operational emissions reduction (Scope 1/2) and climate resilience with specific initiatives including renewable energy collaboration, infrastructure optimization, and TCFD adoption; includes near-term actions (e.g., energy-efficient cooling) and long-term targets (2030); governance and ISO certification goals provide structural support.",
      "status": null
    },
