      "summary": "GuocoLand’s 2023 decarbonization strategy is structured around progressive carbon reduction through operational refinement, supply chain collaboration, and alignment with regulatory frameworks. The company has advanced beyond initial carbon inventory assessments to focus on refining emissions accounting, establishing baselines, and setting actionable targets as part of its decarbonization plan. Key focus areas include integrating climate risk management into site sourcing, reducing embodied carbon across the value chain, and adopting standardized reporting frameworks to ensure transparency and accountability. \n\nTo implement this strategy, GuocoLand is actively refining emissions accounting processes and identifying feasible emission reduction initiatives (AEIs) to lower its carbon footprint. The company is adopting sustainability reporting aligned with TCFD recommendations, treating it as an ongoing process requiring continuous refinement. Additionally, it is exploring the feasibility of committing to Science-Based Targets (SBTi) to align with global climate initiatives. In supply chain management, GuocoLand collaborates with stakeholders to minimize embodied carbon emissions and supports the Singapore Green Building Council’s Embodied Carbon Pledge, demonstrating sector-wide commitment. \n\nFor development projects, the company integrates climate risk and opportunity assessments into site sourcing decisions, working with qualified consultants to address physical risks (e.g., floods, heat waves) and transition risks (e.g., policy changes). It also aligns with government-led initiatives such as Singapore’s Green Plan 2030 and China’s 2030 carbon peak action plan, leveraging policy synergies to enhance decarbonization efforts. These actions collectively form a comprehensive approach that balances operational adjustments with external collaboration to advance sustainable development.",
