      "summary": "Halcyon Agri's decarbonization strategy for 2023 centers on establishing a science-based net-zero pathway with concrete near-term actions. The company has completed a group-wide GHG baseline assessment for Halcyon Rubber Company, Corrie MacColl Plantations, and Corrie MacColl International to establish their current emissions profile. This foundational work supports their commitment to setting science-based net-zero targets by 2025, with specific targets to be secured in accordance with Science Based Targets Initiative (SBTi) requirements. The company is actively developing transition plans to renewable energy sources for all factories where feasible, demonstrating practical implementation through initiatives like dryer retrofitting that provides operational flexibility to combust natural gas or biomass alongside, or as a replacement to liquid fuels.\n\nTo strengthen their strategic approach, Halcyon Agri has conducted climate scenario analysis in accordance with TCFD recommendations, which was completed in 2023. This analysis helps evaluate potential climate impacts and informs their risk management framework. The company is shifting to renewable fuel sources to decrease carbon footprint across operations and supply chain, while implementing specific efficiency measures to reduce manufacturing costs and CO2 emissions. Their strategy integrates climate-related risks into existing risk management systems, with the Board of Directors providing oversight on climate-related topics during quarterly meetings.\n\nSupporting these efforts, Halcyon Agri has established a comprehensive reporting framework aligned with TCFD recommendations, disclosing their group-wide carbon footprint including Scope 3 emissions for the first time in this report. The company is also working to develop a climate mitigation strategy that addresses both physical and transition risks, with a focus on improving business resiliency and adaptability in climate change. These initiatives form part of their broader commitment to achieving carbon neutrality and contributing to a circular economy, with annual communication of climate-related performance to stakeholders.",
