    "strategy": {
      "summary": "The company's decarbonization strategy for 2023 is structured around a three-pillar approach: REDUCE, PRODUCE, and NEUTRALISE, forming the core of their climate change transition plan. The company has committed to reducing absolute Scope 2 GHG emissions by 30% by FY 2035, using FY 2022 as the baseline year as established in their 'SR22 Reporting Boundary.' Recognizing that Scope 1 GHG emissions constitute less than 1% of their total emissions, the company has deferred specific target setting for Scope 1 until these emissions become material. The strategic approach prioritizes reducing emissions within operations first, followed by the supply chain, before addressing residual emissions through renewable energy generation and carbon offset mechanisms.\n\nUnder the REDUCE pillar, the company is implementing specific initiatives focused on energy efficiency across machinery and equipment, motor vehicles, cooling systems, and lighting. Additional focus areas include building design optimization, local supply chain development, clean energy adoption, and electric vehicle integration. For the PRODUCE pillar, the company is concentrating on on-site generation of renewable energy, with solar energy identified as a primary focus area. The NEUTRALISE pillar addresses unavoidable residual emissions through renewable energy certificates (RECs) and carbon credits, creating a comprehensive approach to achieving their decarbonization goals.\n\nThe company tracks and monitors Scope 1, 2, and certain Scope 3 GHG emissions categories, while developing mechanisms to track additional Scope 3 emissions where relevant. They have established a structured climate change transition plan that will be refined and improved as they progressively implement it, considering changes in business operations, environment, and market trends. Progress updates on this decarbonization journey will be provided in their sustainability reports, with assurance on the reporting process covered by an internal review.",
      "notes": "Strategy is well-structured with specific focus areas across three strategic levers. The company has set a concrete target for Scope 2 emissions reduction (30% by FY 2035) but has deferred Scope 1 targets due to their small proportion of total emissions. Strategy focuses primarily on operational emissions with clear implementation pathways outlined for each lever. The document provides specific focus areas but limited implementation details beyond these categories.",
      "status": null
    },
