      "summary": "The company’s decarbonization strategy for 2023 is anchored in science-aligned targets and operational transformation, aiming for Net Zero Carbon across Scope 1 and 2 emissions by 2025 and Absolute Zero Carbon by 2040, with validation from the Science Based Targets initiative (SBTi) confirming alignment with a 1.5°C trajectory. Central to this approach is the elimination of fossil fuels across business operations and the advancement of fossil fuel-free construction practices, emphasizing a transition toward renewable energy and low-carbon technologies. The strategy prioritizes tangible operational shifts to reduce direct emissions while maintaining a clear pathway for long-term decarbonization.\n\nTo operationalize these goals, the company is implementing concrete initiatives such as increasing the use of electric construction equipment and adopting renewable diesel as a transition fuel where available. A flagship project includes the geothermal heat exchange system at 1 Java Street, an all-electric building recognized as the largest geothermal residential system in New York State, demonstrating their commitment to scalable decarbonization solutions. Additionally, the #MissionZero campaign was launched to mobilize internal and external efforts toward achieving the 2025 carbon targets, while quarterly progress reports ensure accountability and transparency in tracking emission reductions.\n\nSupporting this strategy, the Board receives regular updates on sustainability target progress, integrating decarbonization into governance frameworks. The SBTi validation of their Mission Zero targets further solidifies the credibility of their science-based approach, ensuring that operational changes—from equipment electrification to geothermal infrastructure—directly contribute to long-term climate goals. This structured oversight, combined with targeted campaigns and infrastructure projects, reflects a cohesive effort to translate climate commitments into actionable, measurable outcomes.",
