    "strategy": {
      "summary": "The company’s 2023 decarbonization strategy is anchored in science-based targets and a 1.5°C pathway, focusing on operational efficiency, renewable energy adoption, and supply chain engagement. As a Science Based Targets Initiative (SBTi) signatory, it committed to a Net Zero target in 2023 and maintained SBTi-validated <2°C targets since 2019. The strategy emphasizes collaboration, including partnerships with Schneider Electric to develop decarbonization roadmaps for processing operations and participation in global initiatives like COP27’s commodity-linked deforestation roadmap and COP28’s Regenerative Landscapes Action Agenda, which aims to accelerate regenerative agriculture practices. \n\nKey operational initiatives include transitioning to solar power, with a 713 KWp solar farm at a Nigerian rice mill (replacing natural gas) and multiple large solar farms in advanced planning stages. The company implemented a waste heat recovery system at a Nigerian flour and pasta facility, utilizing generator waste heat for steam production to reduce natural gas and diesel use, and commissioned a 1.3 MW cogeneration plant in Nigeria that converts rice husks into energy. Fuel-based forklifts were also replaced with electric ones at an integrated feed and protein facility in Nigeria. These efforts are supported by biomass, which accounted for 51% of total energy consumption in 2023, and a focus on energy intensity measured via gigajoules per metric tonne of product processed. \n\nTo address Scope 3 emissions—which represent over 90% of total GHG emissions (83.01 million tCO₂e)—the company developed product-specific sustainability strategies (Cocoa Compass, Coffee LENS, Nut Trail, Dairy Tracks) to align group targets with the 1.5°C pathway. Climate risk management is institutionalized through the Integrated Risk and Assurance Framework, and the company reports annually to the Carbon Disclosure Project. These actions reflect a comprehensive approach integrating operational changes, technology adoption, and supply chain collaboration to drive decarbonization.",
      "notes": "Multi-page strategy section found; strategy covers operational, supply chain, and partnership elements with specific projects and metrics. Focus on 1.5°C pathway, SBTi alignment, and Scope 3 emissions management.",
      "status": null
    },
