      "summary": "OUE REIT's decarbonization strategy for 2023 centers on operational efficiency, renewable energy integration, and tenant engagement within its portfolio, with a particular focus on properties in Singapore and Shanghai. The company is implementing concrete energy efficiency measures across its buildings, including exploring smart energy solutions at OUE Bayfront and OUE Downtown Office, installing automated meter reading systems, and optimizing operational practices such as switching off non-essential lighting and adjusting swimming pool circulation hours. To reduce carbon intensity, OUE REIT is progressively replacing T5 lighting with energy-efficient LED lighting across office premises, tenant and common areas, and has installed solar panels on the roof of One Raffles Place Tower 2, with plans to expand this initiative in FY 2024. The company also maintains strong focus on green certifications, with Crowne Plaza Changi Airport achieving BCA Green Mark Gold certification and Lippo Plaza pursuing LEED certification renewal. To support these efforts, OUE REIT has implemented a Green Procurement Policy that integrates environmental considerations during project development and established a Green Clause in tenancy agreements requiring tenants to share energy, water, and waste generation data. The company is actively engaging tenants through regular discussions, the 'Green Guide for Tenants,' and green leases that account for approximately 50.3% of the Singapore commercial segment net lettable area. In 2023, OUE REIT conducted a strategic target calibration exercise to evaluate the feasibility and ambition of existing environmental targets, while aligning its climate reporting with IFRS ISSB S2 standards to enhance transparency around climate-related financial disclosures.",
