    "strategy": {
      "summary": "UOB's decarbonization strategy for 2023 is built on a comprehensive approach that balances sector-specific transition pathways with robust governance structures. The bank has committed to supporting a just transition in Southeast Asia, recognizing that climate transition cannot be homogenous across sectors or markets. This approach is underpinned by their operational carbon neutrality, achieved in 2021 for Scope 1, 2, and business air travel emissions, and their adoption of sector-specific targets aligned with international best practices including the Glasgow Financial Alliance for Net Zero (GFANZ) and Science Based Targets initiative (SBTi). The strategy focuses on three main pillars: financing the transition through targeted sustainable finance frameworks, managing climate-related risks through scenario analysis, and leading by example through operational decarbonization.\n\nThe bank has implemented several concrete initiatives to advance decarbonization. UOB exceeded its sustainable finance target by achieving $44.5 billion in portfolio value by the end of 2023, surpassing their $30 billion by 2025 goal. They developed five specific sustainable finance frameworks covering green building, smart cities, circular economy, trade finance, and transition finance to support clients across different sectors. For operational decarbonization, they deployed energy efficiency measures including LED lighting systems and smart building sensors, sourced renewable energy through high-quality certificates, and utilized carbon offsets for remaining emissions. Additionally, UOB implemented a thermal coal exclusion policy, excluding companies deriving ≥20% revenue from thermal coal mining without transition plans, and limiting portfolio weight to 10% for companies with transition policies. The bank also partnered with DHL to reduce the carbon footprint of international shipping activities and began deploying sustainable aviation fuels through DHL's GoGreen Plus programme.\n\nTo support these initiatives, UOB has established robust governance structures and capacity building programs. The Board approved the UOB Group Sustainability Framework and sustainability report disclosures, while the Management Executive Committee (MEC) and Group Sustainability Committee (GSC) oversee implementation. In 2023, they established a Sustainability Advisory Panel to provide external perspectives on their strategy. All employees completed the mandatory Sustainability 101 e-learning module, and the bank linked remuneration to sustainability performance through the Group Balanced Scorecard. UOB also developed a climate scenario analysis methodology to assess both transition and physical climate risks, and conducted a consulting project to assess Scope 3 non-financed emissions to identify priority areas for stakeholder engagement. These integrated approaches ensure that decarbonization is embedded across the organization's operations, financing activities, and risk management frameworks.",
      "notes": "Multi-page strategy section found across multiple images. Strategy focuses on both operational decarbonization and financing the transition. Specific implementation details provided for 2023 including achieved targets, concrete policies, and partnership initiatives. Strategy demonstrates sector-specific approach with measurable outcomes.",
      "status": null
    },
