    "strategy": {
      "summary": "UOB's decarbonization strategy for 2023 is structured around a comprehensive approach that addresses both operational emissions and financed emissions through a combination of direct action, sustainable finance, and strategic portfolio management. The bank has already achieved operational carbon neutrality across Scope 1, 2, and business air travel emissions (Scope 3) in 2021 and maintains this through a three-pillar approach: energy efficiency upgrades across facilities (including LED lighting systems, smart building sensors, and air conditioning optimization), procurement of renewable energy through high-quality Energy Attribute Certificates and international standards like I-REC and TIGR, and high-quality carbon offsets registered with the Gold Standard and Verified Carbon Standard. For its financed emissions, UOB has implemented a robust sustainable finance strategy that has already exceeded its 2025 target, achieving a $44.5 billion sustainable finance portfolio by the end of 2023 through five specialized financing frameworks designed for specific sectors including green building, smart cities, circular economy, sustainable trade, and transition finance.\n\nThe bank has established clear environmental policies for high-risk sectors, particularly thermal coal, with exclusion criteria for companies deriving more than 20% of revenue from thermal coal mining without transition plans, and a 10% portfolio weight limitation for companies with transition plans. For its real estate portfolio, UOB developed a decarbonization roadmap that includes energy conservation measures and power purchase agreements, and conducted a 2023 consulting project to assess Scope 3 non-financed emissions to identify priority areas. The bank also partnered with DHL since 2022 to reduce the carbon footprint of international shipping activities, with plans to implement DHL's GoGreen Plus program in 2024 for sustainable aviation fuels across all global consignments.\n\nSupporting these initiatives is a strong governance framework, with the Board reviewing and approving the sustainability framework and report disclosures in 2023, while management committees (MEC and GSC) oversee implementation. The bank established a Sustainability Advisory Panel to provide external perspectives and linked employee remuneration to sustainability performance through the Group Balanced Scorecard. All employees completed the mandatory Sustainability 101 e-learning module, and the bank has integrated sustainability metrics into KPIs and appraisal processes. UOB also employs climate scenario analysis methodology to assess both transition and physical risk scenarios, using scenario-adjusted financial statements to inform risk management decisions across its portfolio.",
      "notes": "Multi-page strategy section found across multiple pages of the report. Strategy focuses on both operational emissions and financed emissions with specific implementation details. Strategy includes concrete targets, frameworks, and measurement approaches. Well-structured with governance, implementation, and sector-specific components. Strong emphasis on just transition in ASEAN region.",
      "status": null
    },
